<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Campbelltown Hospital Research — mission, how the site works, and governance links."
>
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="wrap page-header__inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>About this site</h1>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section wrap-narrow" data-pagefind-body>
    <h2>Mission</h2>
    <p>
      Campbelltown Hospital Research exists to be a single, elegant, always-current home for
      research at Campbelltown Hospital: a public showcase of publications, clinical trials,
      research groups and news, and a discovery engine for students and JMOs looking for a
      topic, a supervisor and a project that fits their term, their skills and their time
      budget.
    </p>
    <p>
      The publication wall, trial listings and researcher profiles are designed to update
      themselves from authoritative sources — PubMed and ClinicalTrials.gov today, with ORCID
      and other registries under consideration — so the site stays current without relying on
      anyone remembering to hand-edit a page. Humans curate: adding narrative, reviewing
      auto-drafted content, and deciding what's ready to publish.
    </p>
    <p>
      This is an independent, clinician-led pilot, not an official SWSLHD website. It follows
      the precedent set by other SWSLHD-adjacent resources hosted outside core NSW Health web
      infrastructure (the Clinical Library's LibGuides site, the Ingham Institute's own
      website): build something useful quickly, demonstrate its value, and pursue formal
      endorsement with a working product in hand.
    </p>

    <h2>How the site works</h2>
    <p>
      The site is a static website: every page is generated at build time from structured
      content and data files, then published as plain HTML, CSS and a small amount of
      JavaScript for filtering and search. There is no database and no server to maintain.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Publications</strong> are harvested from PubMed by an automated pipeline that
        searches for Campbelltown Hospital affiliations, normalises the metadata, and tags
        each paper by department. Papers with a Campbelltown-based first, last or
        corresponding author are badged "Campbelltown-led".
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Clinical trials</strong> are synced from the ClinicalTrials.gov v2 API,
        filtered to trials with a Campbelltown Hospital facility.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Researcher profiles</strong> are auto-stubbed from public PubMed data, then
        only published once the researcher has confirmed — a quick consent step — that they're
        happy to appear.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>News and student projects</strong> are curated directly by the research office
        and supervisors.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Every automated update arrives as a reviewable change, not a silent one — nothing
      publishes without a clear audit trail.
    </p>

